        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.707,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Geometric Twins"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.664,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "Similarly, the sides AB and BC are equal. So $\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{C}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.108,
            0.847,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "So, all the three angles of an equilateral triangle are equal, just like their sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.155,
            0.46,
            0.178
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What could be their measures?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.188,
            0.67,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "As the three angles should add up to 180°, we have 3 × angle in an equilateral triangle = 180°. So each angle is 60°."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.254,
            0.419,
            0.278
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Verify this by construction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.287,
            0.846,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "Thus, just using the notion of congruence, we have deduced that the angles of an equilateral triangle are all 60°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.326,
            0.847,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": "**Congruent Triangles in Real Life:** Congruent triangles can be seen in various constructions and designs from ancient to modern times. Here are a few examples."
        },
